cocoa-ui source provenance

This directory is the tracked source tree of the water-rs/cocoa-ui
repository — the safe, idiomatic Rust API over AppKit and UIKit the
native Apple backend binds through — imported without git ancestry.
The original repository is ARCHIVED and retains its full source history.
Maintenance and native validation now live in water-rs/waterui at
backends/apple/cocoa-ui (archival recorded in WaterUI issue #1450).

Imported source — byte-identical to upstream `dev` at:

  03cc55e1973581f2c9966e80c81b773da1db9898 — Cocoa#12, the merged
  private native-cache device binding (signed head 70de15a, full CI
  run 37090423845 green before merge).

Reconciliation at import time: no open pull requests and no unique
work on any upstream branch — `origin/feat/281-objc2-contract`,
`origin/feat/appkit-window-extras` and `origin/main` each hold zero
commits ahead of `origin/dev`, verified via `git log origin/dev..<branch>`.

Files imported: `src/` (123 files), `tests/native/`, `examples/`
(smoke fixtures), `Cargo.toml`, `README.md`, `LICENSE-APACHE`,
`LICENSE-MIT`.

Deliberate manifest adjustments on import (source unchanged):

  - `repository` repointed to water-rs/waterui and `publish = false`
    added, matching this repository's platform-backend policy.
  - `[patch.crates-io]` removed: the workspace root carries the same
    eleven water-rs/wgpu entries at the identical rev `4b35d8bc…`,
    so resolution is unchanged and the wgpu 30 fork pins are preserved.

Excluded from the import: `.git`, `Cargo.lock` (the workspace lock
owns resolution), `.github/` (CI coverage transfers to this
repository's apple.yml and apple-e2e.yml workflows), `.cargo/config.toml` and `.github/scripts/nextest-ios-sim.sh`
(the root `.cargo/config.toml` and `.github/scripts/nextest-ios-sim.sh`
already supply the equivalent `aarch64-apple-ios-sim` runner, keyed by
`WATERUI_IOS_SIM_UDID`), `.gitignore`, `AGENTS.md`, and every generated
or build output.

The `waterui-apple` crate now depends on this member by path; the
crate name, public API, feature granularity (`map`/`avkit`/`webview`),
lint set and explicit dependency declarations are unchanged.

Imported nonempty text files missing a terminal newline were normalized during signed integration; source behavior is unchanged.
